  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `add_tag`, and `python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py` now passes.\n\nThe problem was the default `tags=[]`. Python creates that list once and reuses it, so tags from one call showed up in later calls that didn't pass `tags`. The default is now `tags=None`, and the function starts a new empty list when `tags` isn't given.\n\nIf a caller passes their own list, `add_tag` still adds the tag to that same list rather than a copy. I checked this with a quick run. `remove_tag` and `test_public.py` are unchanged.\n\nDONE: Changed `add_tag`'s default from `tags=[]` to `tags=None` so each call without `tags` starts with a new list; public test passes.",
