      "final_message": "I rewrote `solution.py` to follow the README. Both public tests pass when I run `python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py`.\n\nThe rewritten `semver_compare(a, b)` does four things:\n- **Non-string input:** raises `TypeError`.\n- **Format check:** each version must match `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` exactly, using plain digits with no leading zeros. Anything else raises `ValueError`. This includes pre-release tags, a trailing newline, leading spaces, non-ASCII digits and empty strings.\n- **Comparison:** it compares `(major, minor, patch)` as integer tuples, so `0.10.0` counts as greater than `0.9.0`.\n- **Result:** returns `-1`, `0` or `1`.\n\nI also ran some quick extra checks beyond the public tests: equal versions, greater versions, and a set of bad strings and non-string values. All behaved as the README says.\n\nDONE: Rewrote `semver_compare` to check strict `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` format (`TypeError` for non-strings, `ValueError` for bad strings) and compare as integer tuples; public tests pass.",
